What is Kubernates ? 
  Kubernates is a orchastration platform  that automates the deployment, management and scaling of containerized applications.

  Kubernates will be installed on a server. It consists of multiple clusters. Each cluster will have multiple nodes. A cluster consistes of master node and worker node.

  Master Node - manages all the componets with in the cluster.
  Worker Node - Node where the contarized application run and communicates the status and other info to the master node using kubectl.

Master Node components - API Server, etcd, Scheduler, controller, Kubernates
Worker Node Components - Kubectl, container runtime (Docker etc), kubernates

API Server - All the interation s to the cluser flows though api server.
etcd - consists of cluster information in key value pairs
Scheduler - Assigns the containers to Nodes
Controllers - Spins up the new containers

Kubectl - interacts with the master node and provides all the info about the node and ensure the node is running according to the config
